Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> When I want to speed safely through an explored level, I like to use the _ 
> command to get to the stairs, an altar or the nearest fountain. One of the 
> things I've discovered is the fact that it doesn't acknowledge sinks or 
> gravestones as a feature of the dungeon.

Works for me.

You might got confused since gravestones are represented by the same
character as vertical walls and sinks are represented by the same
character as corridors. So whenever you locate these characters you'll
be pointed sequentially, line by line, from one wall (resp. corridor)
segment to the next.

I think the travel command could be enhanced to ignore corridors and
walls and restrict to the more specific dungeon features. OTOH, these
two features are rare. The most important are the stairs/ladders, then
altars, and maybe traps as waypoints.

> A gravestone usually becomes a pit. A sink can become a fountain.
> Just curious why they can't be used as waypoints or destinations with _.

